msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We released Quarkus 3.14.2, a maintenance release for our 3.14 release train."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It contains several important bugfixes so we recommend the upgrade for "
"anyone already using 3.14."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While our maintenance releases usually don't include important changes, we "
"had to make an exception for the upgrade to Micrometer 1.13."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Our main issue was that Micrometer 1.12 would reach EOL in a few months, "
"which wasn't in line with the upcoming 3.15 LTS release.\n"
"As previously explained, 3.15 will be based the continuation of the 3.14 "
"branch,\n"
"thus why we included this update in 3.14."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3."
"14#micrometer[3.14 migration guide] has been updated to reflect that."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.14, we recommend updating to the latest version of "
"the Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.14."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about the adjustments you need to make to your "
"applications, please refer to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/"
"Migration-Guide-3.14[Quarkus 3.14 migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/3.14.2[3.14.2] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come Join Us"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... "
"Let's build something great together!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our "
"welcoming community:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https:/"
"/groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/"
"quarkus[Stack Overflow]."
msgstr ""
